Z||000000||MooCow||07-18-2000||11:56 PM||||Can someone please tell me what these are and where to find them and how much they are and how hard they are to install????<BR>         <BR>                                  Thanks Ken<P>||||reg||5
Z||000001||stimpy||07-19-2000||12:22 AM||||Uh-oh, another thread on the touchy subject of ignition upgrades. I'll try not to step on any toes of people with any partcularly strong allegiance to coils or wire manufacturers. But since I am using both products in my car, I figured I'd weigh in on the matter.<P>The SuperCoil is just what you'd think... an ignition coil. My layman's understanding of what a coil does is take that 12v current from the battery and amplify it to create the powerful spark off of the spark plug of your choice (no endorsement intended, hell, use champion if ya want!) The Accell coil is designed to create a larger, hotter spark. Cost is around $45 at your local auto parts store and installs just like the factory coil. I got mine at O'Reilly's. Make sure you do <B>not</B> get the universal model.<P>The Spiral Core wires are just spark plug wires, the method of delivering that spark. There are lots of high quality wires available from many different manufacturers ... Taylor, BorgWarner, etc. I chose Accel over others mostly for cosmetic reasons. I have heard that the basic Accel wires are of dubious quality, but I have had no problems with my wires. They are about $40 for the set. <P>Hopefully this answers your qestion without putting anyone's panties in a <B>B</B>unch. Just don't ask me about spark plugs!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>PS Better Terry? ^ (ya goofball!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )<BR>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://gifs123.tripod.com/page15/renstimpy2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by stimpy (edited 07-19-2000).]||||reg||4
